message.content:
Design an implementation plan to unify the admin Live Preview and storefront widget rendering in the Pinzo Shopify app so they use the same HTML structure and CSS classes.

## Current State

The admin preview (`app.widget.tsx`) and storefront widget (`zip-code-checker.liquid`) already share CSS classes for:
- Heading (`.zcc-heading`)
- Search bar + input + button (`.zcc-search-bar`, `.zcc-input`, `.zcc-btn`)
- Error/not-found result (`.zcc-result.fail`)
- Waitlist form (`.zcc-wl`)

But the **success result** diverges completely:
- **Admin**: Uses inline React styles — gradient backgrounds, card-based layout, stat boxes for ETA/Zone, colored rows
- **Storefront**: Uses CSS classes — `.zcc-result.ok`, `.zcc-meta`, `.zcc-cod`, `.zcc-delivery-fee`, `.zcc-countdown`, `.zcc-delivery-date`

The admin shows a polished design that doesn't exist on the storefront.

## Goal

Make the admin preview success result use the SAME CSS classes as the storefront, AND upgrade the storefront CSS to be modern/polished. Result: change CSS in one place → both update.

## Strategy

**Don't move rendering to a shared file** (too complex — one is React JSX, other is JS string building in Liquid). Instead:

1. **Upgrade the storefront CSS** (`buildSharedCss`/`buildWidgetCss` in liquid) to make `.zcc-result.ok` and its children look modern and polished (matching the current admin preview design)
2. **Replace admin preview inline styles** with the same CSS classes the storefront uses
3. Both share the SAME CSS generation functions — admin already calls `buildAdminPreviewCss()` which internally calls `buildWidgetCss()` and `buildSharedMetaCss()` (TypeScript versions that mirror the storefront's JS versions)

## Key insight

The admin preview ALREADY generates and injects the same CSS via `buildAdminPreviewCss()`. It just doesn't USE those classes for the success result — it uses inline styles instead. So the fix is:

1. Make the success result CSS (in `buildWidgetCss`/`buildSharedCss` in BOTH files) look modern
2. Replace the admin's inline-styled success JSX with class-based JSX matching storefront HTML structure

## Specific changes needed

### File 1: Storefront widget CSS — upgrade `.zcc-result.ok` and children
`extensions/zip-code-widget/blocks/zip-code-checker.liquid`

Enhance `buildWidgetCss` and `buildSharedCss` to make the success result look modern:
- `.zcc-result.ok` — add subtle border, rounded corners, overflow hidden
- `.zcc-result.ok .zcc-result-icon` — make it a green circle badge with background
- `.zcc-result.ok .zcc-result-message` — make text green, semibold
- `.zcc-meta` — clean row with icon + text, subtle bottom border, good padding
- `.zcc-delivery-date` — similar to meta but with calendar icon
- `.zcc-countdown` — urgency colors already exist, add padding
- `.zcc-cod--available` — pill badge style (already exists, just ensure it's polished)
- `.zcc-delivery-fee--free` — green pill (already exists)
- `.zcc-return-policy` — subtle footer text

### File 2: Admin preview CSS — mirror changes
`app/routes/app.widget.tsx`

The admin has its own `buildWidgetCss` and `buildSharedMetaCss` TypeScript functions. Update them to match the storefront CSS exactly.

### File 3: Admin preview success JSX — replace inline styles with classes
`app/routes/app.widget.tsx`

Replace the entire success result section (currently ~170 lines of inline-styled divs) with class-based JSX matching the storefront structure:

```jsx
{previewState === "success" && (
  <div className="zcc-result ok">
    <div className="zcc-result-icon">{checkCircleIcon}</div>
    <div className="zcc-result-content">
      <div className="zcc-result-message">{cfg.successMessage}</div>
      {effectiveCfg.showEta && (
        <div className="zcc-meta">{truckIcon}<span>Estimated delivery: <strong>2–3 business days</strong></span></div>
      )}
      {effectiveCfg.showDeliveryDate && effectiveCfg.showEta && (
        <div className="zcc-meta zcc-delivery-date">{calendarIcon}<span>Expected by <strong>Friday, Mar 28</strong></span></div>
      )}
      {effectiveCfg.showZone && (
        <div className="zcc-meta">{locationIcon}<span>Zone: <strong>North</strong></span></div>
      )}
      {effectiveCfg.showDeliveryDays && (
        <div className="zcc-meta zcc-days">{calendarIcon}<span>Mon · Tue · Wed · Thu · Fri</span></div>
      )}
      {effectiveCfg.showCutoffTime && (
        <div className="zcc-meta zcc-cutoff">{clockIcon}<span>Order by <strong>2:00 PM</strong> for same-day</span></div>
      )}
      {effectiveCfg.showCountdown && effectiveCfg.showCutoffTime && (
        <div className="zcc-countdown zcc-countdown--amber">{clockIcon}<span>Order within <strong>2h 14m</strong> for same-day dispatch</span></div>
      )}
      {effectiveCfg.showCod && (
        <div className="zcc-cod zcc-cod--available">{cardIcon} Cash on Delivery Available</div>
      )}
      {effectiveCfg.showDeliveryFee && (
        <div className="zcc-delivery-fee zcc-delivery-fee--free">{truckIcon} Free Delivery</div>
      )}
      {effectiveCfg.showReturnPolicy && (
        <div className="zcc-return-policy">{refreshIcon}<span>7-day easy returns</span></div>
      )}
    </div>
  </div>
)}
```

This is ~30 lines vs the current ~170 lines of inline styles. And it renders EXACTLY what the storefront renders.

## CSS Design for Modern Success Result

Both storefront and admin should have these enhanced CSS rules:

```css
/* Success result card */
.zcc-result.ok {
  background: ${successColor}08;
  border: 1px solid ${successColor}20;
  border-radius: ${borderRadius}px;
  padding: 0;
  overflow: hidden;
}

/* Success icon — green circle */  
.zcc-result.ok .zcc-result-icon {
  background: ${successColor}15;
  border-radius: 50%;
  padding: 6px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
}

/* Success message — green text */
.zcc-result.ok .zcc-result-message {
  color: ${successColor};
  font-weight: 600;
}

/* Meta rows — clean with subtle borders */
.zcc-meta {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  font-size: 13px;
  color: ${textColor};
  padding: 6px 0;
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(0,0,0,0.04);
  line-height: 1.4;
}

/* Last meta item — no border */
.zcc-meta:last-child {
  border-bottom: none;
}
```

## Execution order
1. Upgrade storefront CSS in `buildSharedCss`/`buildWidgetCss` (liquid file)
2. Mirror the same CSS in admin's `buildWidgetCss`/`buildSharedMetaCss` (tsx file)
3. Replace admin success JSX with class-based markup
4. Verify both render identically

## Constraints
- Storefront CSS uses `!important` everywhere (needed for Liquid theme isolation)
- Admin CSS does NOT use `!important` (React scope is sufficient)
- Keep the same HTML structure so both look identical
- Don't change the storefront's JS HTML-building logic — only its CSS
- Don't change the floating/popup/inline preview containers

